      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "E",
      "plays_role": "Signal fidelity is the transmission of the creedal content through the oral tradition without corruption into myth. The paper's central worry is whether the creeds were expanded until they became myth, i.e., whether the signal survived.",
      "quote": "What keeps the creeds from being expanded until they become myth and they're not really the words of the eyewitnesses. [S063]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "S_eff",
      "plays_role": "Effective entropy is the corruption of the oral tradition over time—the expansion of creeds into myth, which would destroy their evidentiary value. The pre-50 dating is precisely what limits this entropy.",
      "quote": "What keeps the creeds from being expanded until they become myth and they're not really the words of the eyewitnesses. [S063]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "T",
      "plays_role": "Temporal integration is the dating window: 30-50 AD, 33-48 AD, or 30-39 AD. The shorter the gap, the stronger the argument. Time is the variable that turns possibility into accumulated consequence.",
      "quote": "Put this way 33 to 48 is only 15 years. [S013]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "K",
      "plays_role": "Compression is the creedal formula itself—a compact summary of the gospel (deity, death, resurrection) that compresses the essential message into transmissible form. The creed is the compression of the eyewitness testimony.",
      "quote": "That's the classic gospel of deity, death, resurrection. [S054]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "R",
      "plays_role": "Phase transition is the conversion of Paul—a discrete event that changes his state from persecutor to apostle and anchors the dating of the creed. It is a threshold, not a degree.",
      "quote": "Now, conservatives and liberals believe that Paul became a Christian two to three years, Bultmann, two to three years after the cross. [S048]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "Q",
      "plays_role": "Superposition is the unresolved dating of the creeds before the evidence is weighed—the open possibility that the creed could be early or late, which is only actualized by the convergence of Paul's timeline and the Jesus Seminar's admission.",
      "quote": "I don't know if that if that >> Yeah, I I think Yeah, so you are right. [S034]",
      "fit": "stretched"
    },
    {
      "slot": "F",
      "plays_role": "Non-local correlation is the agreement between conservatives and liberals (including the Jesus Seminar and Bart Ehrman) on the early dating—independent sources that are no longer independent once they converge on the same date.",
      "quote": "Now, conservatives and liberals believe that Paul became a Christian two to three years, Bultmann, two to three years after the cross. [S048]",
